0,Music of Madagascar - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Madagascar,"Music in Madagascar tends toward major keys and diatonic scales, [6] although coastal music makes frequent use of minor keys, most likely due to early Arab influences at coastal ports of call. [7] Malagasy music has served a wide range of social, spiritual and mundane functions across the centuries.","Malagasy, Tesaka",Austronesian
1,Malagasy language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malagasy_language,"A woman speaking Malagasy (1:32) Malagasy (/ ˌmæləˈɡæsi / MAL-ə-GASS-ee; [3] Malagasy pronunciation: [malaˈɡasʲ]; Sorabe: مَلَغَسِ) is an Austronesian language and dialect continuum spoken in Madagascar. The standard variety, called Official Malagasy, is one of the official languages of Madagascar, alongside French. Malagasy is the westernmost Austronesian language, brought ...","Malagasy, Tesaka",Austronesian
2,Madagascar Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh98bHRQ-CBQTWRSC0PNbILd,"Madagasgar, or the Malagasy Republic, was among the first regions of Africa to receive black immigrants from Melanesia in prehistoric times. The ancestors of...","Malagasy, Tesaka",Austronesian
